E10-ISS-01 Refuse to ship when conjunct 2 fails and conjunct 3 passes (A3.9)
base: "an issuance attempt"
mutations: [{"op": "chain_times", "h*": "declared + delta + 1 s", "h*+5": "declared + delta - 1 s"}]
test_universe: {"issue": {"times": {"900024": "TB + DELTA + 1", "900029": "TB + DELTA - 1"}}, "expect": "IssueRefused (pre-ship receipt_c2 = false)"}
staging: {"status": "requires staging harness", "harness": "staging issuer with (a) a header-source stub / simulated chain whose block times the tester sets, (b) a readable attempt log: attempt id, state transitions, per-request attempt counter, ship decision with the conjunct values", "sequence": ["S1 submit request R at staged declared time d; record attempt id A1 and counter n0", "S2 stub mines the anchor block h* with nTime d+DELTA+1", "S3 stub mines h*+1..h*+5 one at a time, h*+5 with nTime d+DELTA-1 (six confirmations, the model's depth 5)", "S4 hold the chain at h*+5 until the issuer records a decision for A1"], "observations": ["O1 the decision record for A1 carries c2 = false (and c1, c3 = true, depth = 6)", "O2 A1 moves to discarded, with no shipped state before or after", "O3 the attempt counter for R reads n0+1 (counted against N)", "O4 no receipt for A1 is returned by the API or present in the issuer's outbox at any point", "O5 the issuer starts attempt A2 (or, if A1 was the N-th, enters the refusal: see E10-ISS-04)"], "controls": [{"id": "C1-ships", "change": "S2 with nTime(h*) = d+DELTA and S3 with nTime(h*+5) = d+DELTA (all conjuncts pass at the boundary)", "expect": "A1 ships; the receipt verifies VALID_STRICT, T = d+DELTA (cf. E10-TMP-06); counter not advanced by a discard"}], "pass": "O1-O4 hold for the refusal run and C1 ships; a refusal without the matching discard and counter observations is NOT a pass", "test_oracle": ["E10-ISS-01.test-refuse", "E10-ISS-01.test-control"], "test_oracle_limit": "The TEST issuer (prototype/conformance/issue.py) only raises IssueRefused with receipt_c2 = false; it has no attempts, discard or N. The oracle fixes the pre-ship decision, not O2-O3."}

E10-ISS-02 Refuse to ship when conjunct 3 fails although wall-clock and burial look done (wall-clock ship guard)
base: "an issuance attempt"
mutations: [{"op": "chain_times", "h*": "declared + delta/2", "h*+5": "declared + 3*delta/2"}, {"op": "wall_clock_at_ship", "value": "declared + delta (inside the wall deadline)"}]
test_universe: {"issue": {"times": {"900024": "TB + 129600", "900029": "TB + 388800"}}, "expect": "IssueRefused (pre-ship receipt_c3 = false)"}
staging: {"status": "requires staging harness", "harness": "staging issuer with the simulated chain of E10-ISS-01 and a lifecycle (wall) clock W the harness drives; the attempt log records W at every event", "sequence": ["S1 W := d; submit request R; record attempt A1 and its lifecycle expiry W_exp = d+DELTA+slack", "S2 W := d+DELTA/2; stub mines h* with nTime d+DELTA/2", "S3 W advances to d+DELTA-3600 (inside the wall deadline); stub mines h*+1..h*+5, h*+5 with nTime d+3*DELTA/2 (six confirmations)", "S4 hold W at d+DELTA-3600 and the chain at h*+5 until A1's decision is recorded"], "observations": ["O1 the decision record for A1 is made at W_dec < W_exp, carries the confirmed proof (h*..h*+5 headers) and c3 = false", "O2 A1 is not marked expired (the refusal is not a lifecycle expiry)", "O3 no receipt for A1 is returned or queued"], "controls": [{"id": "C1-ships", "change": "S3 with nTime(h*+5) = d+DELTA, same W schedule", "expect": "A1 ships at W_dec < W_exp; the receipt verifies VALID_STRICT"}], "pass": "O1-O3 for the refusal run and C1 ships; a ships:false caused by expiry (O2 fails) is NOT a pass", "test_oracle": ["E10-ISS-02.test-refuse", "E10-ISS-02.test-control"], "test_oracle_limit": "The TEST issuer has no wall clock; its oracle fixes only that c3 = false refuses and the c3-boundary control ships."}

E10-ISS-03 Never ship before the sixth confirmation exists
base: "an issuance attempt"
mutations: [{"op": "observe", "detail": "poll the issue API while the anchor has 1..5 confirmations"}]
test_universe: {"issue": {"supply_remove": [900029]}, "expect": "IssueRefused (receipt_anchored = false)"}
staging: {"status": "requires staging harness (live half observable through the public API)", "harness": "staging issuer with the simulated chain; the harness can hold the chain at a chosen depth; API responses and the issuer outbox are logged", "depth_convention": "The model's DepthK = 5 counts successors of the including block (P5c_IssuanceProtocol.tla:202, :262; k6 cfgs DepthK = 5), so shipping needs h*..h*+5: six confirmations.", "sequence": ["S1 submit request R; stub mines h* (1 confirmation)", "S2 for c = 1..5: hold the chain at c confirmations for at least one issuer decision cycle; poll the API and read the outbox", "S3 release the sixth confirmation (h*+5)"], "observations": ["O1 at every hold c = 1..5: no receipt in any API response and none in the outbox", "O2 after S3: a receipt is returned; its headers hold h*..h*+5 for the receipt, snapshot and git proofs, and it verifies VALID_STRICT", "O3 (simulated reorg, optional) orphaning h* during S2 produces no receipt and a new attempt"], "controls": [{"id": "C1-release", "change": "S3 itself", "expect": "the receipt ships only after the sixth confirmation (O2)"}], "public_api_only": "Through the public API alone only O2's bundle half is checkable: any returned receipt must hold h*..h*+5 for all three proofs. Polling cannot exclude a premature shipment.", "pass": "O1 and O2", "test_oracle": ["E10-ISS-03.test-refuse", "E10-ISS-03.test-control"], "test_oracle_limit": "The TEST issuer refuses when h*+5's header is absent (receipt_anchored = false). That is evidence completeness, not the live sequence."}

E10-ISS-04 Refusal after N = 3 expired attempts, entered atomically, no receipt
base: "an issuance request"
mutations: [{"op": "fault", "detail": "OTS calendars unreachable (or never confirming) for 3 x (delta + slack)"}]
test_universe: null
staging: {"status": "requires staging harness", "harness": "staging issuer with an OTS calendar fault switch, a compressible lifecycle clock, the attempt log, and a durable refusal record", "sequence": ["S1 calendars unreachable; submit request R at W = d", "S2 advance W past attempt 1's expiry (DELTA + slack); observe expiry and the start of attempt 2", "S3 repeat for attempts 2 and 3", "S4 after attempt 3 expires, observe the refusal", "S5 restore calendar availability and deliver late evidence that would confirm attempt 3's anchor in window", "S6 advance W and poll; restart the issuer process; poll again"], "observations": ["O1 exactly three attempts, each expired at its own W_exp (attempt counter 1, 2, 3)", "O2 the refusal is entered once, at attempt 3's expiry, atomically with the final discard (no state between)", "O3 after S5 and S6 the request R stays refused: no receipt is ever returned and no attempt 4 starts", "O4 the refusal survives the restart (latched)"], "controls": [{"id": "C1-recovers", "change": "restore the calendars during attempt 2", "expect": "attempt 2 ships; no refusal is entered (RefusedOnlyWhenExhausted)"}, {"id": "C2-stalled", "change": "freeze W during an outage", "expect": "no refusal and no expiry: distinguishes a latched refusal from a stalled issuer"}], "pass": "O1-O4 and both controls", "test_oracle": [], "test_oracle_limit": "No TEST issuer recipe: issue.py has no attempts, clock or refusal latch."}

