E10-SP2-04 Attacker material in the gpg slot under the honest manifest -> KEY_MISMATCH (gpg)
base: "honest bundle (A-a)"
mutations: [{"op": "replace_slot_material", "slot": "gpg", "with": "attacker key: keys.gpg, F_gpg signer.key_fp, S_gpg, possession.gpg"}, {"op": "keep", "what": "honest manifest"}, {"op": "restamp", "value": "split: subcases .unstamped and .restamped"}]
test_universe: {"hooks": "attacker gpg key for slot material; manifest built for the honest gpg key; adversarial=True"}
subcase: {"id": "E10-SP2-04.restamped", "title": "TEST form: re-stamped", "construction": "TEST issue, adversarial; gpg slot material (keys.gpg, F_gpg signer.key_fp, S_gpg, possession.gpg) from attacker key e10-attacker-gpg; manifest names the honest gpg key; DNS names the honest keys; A_sig stamped"}
subcase: {"id": "E10-SP2-04.unstamped", "title": "L0/L1 form: not re-stamped", "construction": "A-a; post-issue: keys.gpg, possession.gpg and the a_sig gpg pair replaced by the attacker material of .restamped; receipt_anchor kept (the L0/L1 form)"}

E10-SP2-05 Honest frames with a substituted manifest -> RECEIPT_MANIFEST_MISMATCH
base: "honest bundle (A-a)"
mutations: [{"op": "replace_member", "path": "manifest", "with": "F_manifest with sset = [another valid gpg fingerprint]"}]
test_universe: {"post_edit": "rebuild F_manifest with another fingerprint; keep a_sig"}
subcase: {"id": "E10-SP2-05", "construction": "A-a; post-issue: manifest replaced by F_manifest with sset = [fp of TEST key other-gpg]; a_sig kept"}

E10-SP2-06 Content splice: each slot honestly signs different content -> RECEIPT_COMMON_MISMATCH
base: "honest bundle (A-a)"
mutations: [{"op": "frames_set", "field": "common.content", "value": {"TEST": "other content"}, "slots": "gpg", "resign": "service gpg key"}]
test_universe: {"hooks": "common_slots hook: common_gpg.content differs; both frames signed honestly"}
subcase: {"id": "E10-SP2-06.L3", "title": "L3 form: one issue, slots sign different content", "construction": "TEST issue, adversarial; common_slots hook: the gpg frame's common.content = {TEST: 'other content'}; both frames signed honestly; A_sig stamped"}
subcase: {"id": "E10-SP2-06.L0", "title": "L0 form: splice two real receipts", "construction": "A-a; post-issue: the a_sig gpg pair replaced by (F_gpg, S_gpg) of a second honest receipt R2 with content {TEST: 'other content'}; receipt_anchor kept"}

E10-SP3-01 Possession transplanted onto another manifest -> POSSESSION_INVALID
